/-!
# Local reductions for recognition with a supplied complement

The explicit complement acts faithfully on the normal elementary subgroup,
which is self-centralizing in the involution centralizer. The Sylow center
has order two. The concrete alternating and Steiner-Mathieu centralizers
are fixed for the remaining identification arguments.

Source: Huppert--Blackburn, *Finite Groups III*, XII.1.18(b), p.314; Held,
"A Characterization of some multiply transitive permutation groups, I",
Illinois J. Math. 13 (1969), 224--240, especially the remark on p.224.

The local model dichotomy and the two global recognition branches remain
unproved. This interface does not yet assert the M22/A10 alternative.
-/
